<title>USA: NORDIC SKIING-JUMPING RESULTS IN NORDIC COMBINED EVENT.</title>
<headline>NORDIC SKIING-JUMPING RESULTS IN NORDIC COMBINED EVENT.</headline>
<dateline>STEAMBOAT SPRINGS, Colorado 1996-12-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Leading</p>
<p>teams Saturday in the 120-metre jumping portion of a World Cup</p>
<p>nordic combined two-man sprint relay at Howelsen Hill (jump</p>
<p>distances in meters):</p>
<p>1. Finland-1 (Jari Mantila, 115.5-97.5 meters/Sampaa</p>
<p>Lajunen, 113-113.5) 222.2 points</p>
<p>2. USA-1 (Tim Tetreault, 112/109.5/Todd Lodwick, 104-98.5)</p>
<p>217.9 (starts 18 seconds back in 15-km)</p>
<p>3. Japan-1 (Futoshi Otake, 113.5-103/Kenji Ogiwara,</p>
<p>104.5-103), 216.4 (0:25 back)</p>
<p>4. Austria-1 Felix Gottwald, 107.5-105.5/Mario Stecher,</p>
<p>109-105) 216.2 (0:26 back)</p>
<p>5. Japan-2 (Kouji Takazawa, 109-109/Tsugihara Ogiwara,</p>
<p>100-99.5) 212.7 (0:45 back)</p>
<p>6. USA-2 (Dave Jarrett, 110-106.5/Ryan Heckman, 97.5-104.5)</p>
<p>211.8 (0:44 back)</p>
<p>7. Norway-1 (Bjarte Engen Vik, 114.5-115.5/Halldor Skard,</p>
<p>104-80) 209.1 (0:56 back)</p>
<p>8. Finland-2 (Hannu Manninen, 105.5-98/Topi Sarparanta,</p>
<p>106.5-101) 206.1 (1:09 back)</p>
<p>9. France-1 (Sylvain Guillaume, 108-106.5/Fabrice Guy,</p>
<p>102-91) 204.2 (1:17 back)</p>
<p>10. Czech Republic-1 (Milan Kucera, 105-91/Ladislav Rygl,</p>
<p>105-101) 201.7 (1:28 back)</p>
</text>
